# The build context for the product image and for the verify image.
#
# This is a correctness file, not a size optimisation. Two entries in it decide
# whether the gate inside the container is checking the same tree a developer has,
# and one decides whether the image can be built at all on a machine with no
# Docker daemon credentials.

# `dist/` is gate OUTPUT. Shipping it into the verify image would let the gate
# read its own previous run's records and pass on them — `TestAGateThatHasNever
# FailedIsNamed` reads `dist/verification/*.json` and asserts every gate has been
# recorded red, so copying the records in would make that assertion vacuous.
#
# This exact defect class is why `scripts/verify.ps1` refuses to overwrite a
# verdict that says PASS without `--force`: a gate that can be satisfied by a file
# somebody copied into it is not a gate.
dist/

# Coverage output, `__pycache__`, and the local artefacts a Windows run leaves.
coverage
coverage.*
*.out
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.test
*.exe

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# `.git` is deliberately KEPT.
#
# The obvious move is to exclude it, and `-buildvcs=false` in the Dockerfile is
# what stops it embedding a revision stamp. Excluding it anyway would be a
# second, quieter reason the binary differs by build context — and it would cost
# the `tree-state` gate its input, so inside the container that gate would report
# "no git" instead of a dirty-file list. A gate that reports nothing because its
# input was stripped from the image is a gate nobody reads.
#
# `.git` reaches the BUILD stage and the VERIFY stage only. The runtime image
# copies `/out` and the data directories, never `/src`, so no `.git` ships to a
# site.

# Local secrets. A `.env` in the build context is a secret in the image, and this
# repository has a `dist/` that a developer may have populated with real
# credentials during the live Pentest. There are no committed `.pem`, `.key` or
# `.env` files â€” checked, not assumed â€” so excluding them by glob costs the gate
# nothing.
.env
.env.*

# Large build-context junk that slows the image build without adding anything
# the runtime or verify images need.
web/spa/node_modules/
web/spa/playwright-report/
web/spa/test-results/
web/static/spa/
*.exe
yolo11x.pt
record.log
record2.log
inc_*.incident.json
inc_*.observation.json
.venv-poc/
